  "chapter": 498,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 18 Chapter 498\n\n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 9259-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  education  law, in relation to authorizing\n        massage therapists licensed in other  jurisdictions  to  perform\n        massage   demonstrations  as  part  of  a  continuing  education\n        program\"\n\n        MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 9928, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the education law,  in  relation  to  licensing  to\n        practice acupuncture\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  Assembly  Bill  9259-A  would authorize massage therapists licensed in\nanother state or country to teach and  demonstrate  \"hands  on\"  massage\ntherapy  techniques  and  modalities  to New York State licensed massage\ntherapists  at  continuing  education  programs  conducted  by  approved\nproviders.\n\n    Assembly Bill 9928 would authorize acupuncturists licensed in anoth-\ner  state  or  country to provide clinical instruction or demonstrations\nand to conduct clinical research at New York State  registered  acupunc-\nture programs.\n\n    Both  of  these  bills  would provide for a limited exemption to New\nYork State licensure requirements in order to ensure an adequate  supply\nof  qualified personnel is available to perform the defined functions in\nNew York. These bills, however, contain several minor technical defects.\nThe Legislature has agreed to pass legislation to address these defects,\nthereby ensuring that the State Education Department can implement these\nlaws in a manner consistent with best practices  and  protecting  public\nsafety. On that basis, I am signing these bills.\n\n  These bills are approved.                   (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
